# Zoom speaking notes — LOCKED

When the user asks for a **script**, talking points, what to say, or notes for a
hearing / CMC / Zoom appearance:

- Copy `.claude/skills/hearing-script/TEMPLATE.md`. Fill the brackets. Delete unused gates.
- Match density/voice to the worked example in `.claude/skills/hearing-script/SKILL.md`.
- Render it **in the chat**, verbose, horizontal rules between sections.
- **Bold on its own line** = Opening / Close / If the Attorney General… / If they say… / If the Court asks… He does not speak that line.
- Regular type under it = the read-aloud. Full sentences. "Your Honor" belongs here.
- Never bury "If the Court" or "If the AG" in the same paragraph as speech.
- Do not shrink to a cue card. Do not use `(don't say)` telegrams.

Portfolio-wide. The August 28, 2026 CHP demurrer is why it exists, not its only case.
